  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2019, the CEACR noted with satisfaction that &quot;...children are no longer involved in the cotton harvest and the systematic or systemic child labour is no longer a matter of concern. School children and students were not mobilized for cotton picking in the 2018 cotton harvest.&quot; The ILO Third-Party Monitoring (TPM) project for child labour and forced labour, which has been monitoring the cotton harvest on an annual basis since 2015, has consistently registered a reduction in the use of child labour during the harvest. Consecutive TPM reports credit the measures taken by the Government to address this issue, which are based mostly on recommendations made by the ILO. The 2018 TPM report noted that the systematic or systemic use of child labour during the cotton harvest is no longer a concern.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2.1. Number of cases of progress in the application of ratified Conventions noted with satisfaction by the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The President of Uzbekistan signed the Law on the ratification of the Promotional Framework for Occupational Safety and Health Convention, 2006 (No. 187) on 4 June 2021. Ratification was registered on 14 September 2021. In 2020, the ILO provided advisory services to constituents to facilitate the ratification of C187.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.2. Number of ratifications of up-to-date technical Conventions, including those recommended by the Governing Body in the context of the Standards Review Mechanism</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
